    {
      "title": "Finished",
      "desc": "One round trip, then data",
      "detail": "The browser sends its own Finished: a check value over everything both sides said, keyed with the new secret, so any tampering with the hellos would show. TLS 1.3 needs one round trip before data flows; TLS 1.2 needed two.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Round trips",
          "1 (TLS 1.2: 2)"
        ],
